# Iterative deepening expectations from fisher-5sg.13, 2026-11-24.
# Scores and per-ply counts independently enumerated with python-chess 1.11.2
# (https://pypi.org/project/chess/1.11.2/) using fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7.
# Decision 10 sums the per-ply counts within each search, then adds the
# nodes from every earlier finished depth of this go. Starting-position
# counts match expectations/perft.epd. D28 sets the default depth to 4.
# The derivation script and results are on fisher-5sg.13.
# Four-ply info spelling from Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), read 2026-11-24:
# UCIEngine::on_update_full in src/uci.cpp and SearchManager::output_pv in src/search.cpp.
# fisher-r6y D41 sets this spelling; fisher-8hc.6 committed these sessions.
# D3-D6 supply the
# existing principal variation and allowances, with time at least one under D41.
# The fisher-2aj.2 sources below supply the retained scores and response order;
# fisher-5sg.13 derived the node totals.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions from 2026-11-22.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7 and 10. Exact search values
# were checked by exhaustive enumeration with python-chess 1.11.2.
# Starting score: four-ply minimax with python-chess 1.11.2 followed rules
# 1 to 7. An independent reviewer reproduced cp 0 and per-ply counts
# 20/400/8902/197281 with their own minimax. See expectations/perft.epd.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
# UCI position and move format. e5d6 is en passant, and e1g1 castles.
> position startpos moves e2e4 a7a6 e4e5 d7d5 e5d6 e7e6 g1f3 g8f6 f1e2 f8e7 e1g1
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes; time, nps and pv as in the header.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 30 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 911 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 27146 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 804607 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# UCI bestmove. The reply carries a legal move in the current position.
< bestmove {legal}
# UCI position and move format. The castling rook leaves the h-file.
> position fen 8/6k1/6B1/3B4/5Q2/8/6R1/4K2R w K - 0 1 moves e1g1
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Black must play g7h8, then f4f8 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 64, 58 and 3599 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -2500 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -2500 nodes 66 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 189 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 3911 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The only legal reply fails if the castling rook still attacks h8.
< bestmove g7h8
# UCI position. The en passant capture makes d5 available to the black king.
> position fen 8/8/5B2/3pP1K1/4k3/8/5Q2/4N3 w - d6 0 1 moves e5d6
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes; time, nps and pv as in the header.
# The second review reproduced the four-ply score cp -2400 and per-ply
# counts 1/40/177/6981 with a shakmaty 0.30.3 minimax.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 42 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 260 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 7459 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The only legal reply fails if the captured pawn stays on d5.
< bestmove e4d5
# UCI position and move format. The pawn promotes to a knight.
> position fen 3Q4/P7/k7/3K4/8/1R6/8/8 w - - 0 1 moves a7a8n
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Black must play a6a7, then d8a5 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 39, 48 and 1923 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -1700 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -1700 nodes 41 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 129 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 2140 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The only legal reply fails if the promotion creates a queen.
< bestmove a6a7
# The next move requires a knight on a8. A bishop cannot reach b6.
> position fen 3Q4/P7/k7/3K4/8/1R6/8/8 w - - 0 1 moves a7a8n a6a7 a8b6
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes; time, nps and pv as in the header.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 2 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 79 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 336 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score {score} nodes 7987 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# Black can play either a7a6 or a7b7 after the full replay.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 8/P7/8/8/8/6q1/5k2/7K w - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. White must promote on a8, then g3h3 is checkmate after any promotion.
# Python-chess counts 4, 102, 848 and 20013 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 4 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 110 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 1064 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 22031 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# UCI move format and bestmove. Every legal move has a promotion suffix.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# The owner accepts an empty moves list as zero moves in fisher-l7f.7.
> position startpos moves
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. See the header for the published perft counts.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 440 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 9762 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 216365 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The starting position replaces the prior position, whose only move is h8g8.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1 moves
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8h7, then g5g7 is checkmate.
# Rules 2 and 3 score the horizon by material, so depths before the mate show material.
# Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 27 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 98 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 1397 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The owner accepts an empty list after FEN too. This position has one legal move.
< bestmove h8h7
> position startpos
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. See the header for the published perft counts.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 440 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 9762 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 216365 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The starting position replaces the prior position, whose only move is h8h7.
< bestmove {legal}
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
